zip.read(path)          // the same record, text when the bytes are UTF-8
tar.write(path, files)
tar.read(path)
```

### Math
```
PI, E                          // Constants, not module members: no math.PI
math.abs(x), math.floor(x), math.ceil(x)
math.round(x), math.sqrt(x), math.pow(x, y)
math.sin(x), math.cos(x), math.tan(x)
math.log(x), math.exp(x)
// every one of them is also spelled flat: abs(x), sqrt(x), ...
// math.random is not implemented, and there is no math.random
```

### Text
```
text.uppercase("text"), text.lowercase("text"), text.trim("text")
text.split("text", by), text.join(list, by)
text.contains("text", sub)
text.starts_with("text", prefix), text.ends_with("text", suffix)
text.replace("text", from, to)
text.length("text")      // characters, not bytes: text.length("héllo") is 5
text.wrap("text", width) // a list of lines no longer than width; whitespace runs become one space
text.diff(old, new)      // a standard unified diff; empty when the texts are equal
text.dedent("text")      // remove the common leading whitespace
text.template("Hi <<name>>!", {name: "Ada"})  // "Hi Ada!"; <<<< writes a literal <<
text.pad("x", 3, "-")    // "x--"
text.align("x", 5, "right")  // "    x"; left, right or center
// uppercase, lowercase, trim, split, join, contains, starts_with, ends_with,
// replace and length are also spelled flat.
```

### Console
```
say "Hello"                      // print with a newline
print "Hello"                    // print without one
console.log("Hello")             // `say` under its module spelling
console.error("Could not read")  // diagnostics go to stderr
console.clear()                  // clear the screen
set name to input("Your name? ")  // read one line from the terminal
```

### Logging
```
logging.set_level("info")          // debug, info, warn, error or off; default off
logging.level()                    // the current threshold
logging.set_timestamps(no)         // deterministic records without a timestamp
logging.set_destination("app.log") // a file path, or "stderr" / "stdout"
logging.debug("looking up a row")
logging.info("read 12 rows")
logging.warn("the cache is cold")
logging.error("the file does not exist")
logging.reset()                    // threshold off, stderr, timestamps on
```

The default threshold is `off`, so a library can call `logging.info` without
changing its caller's output. Records go to stderr unless a file or stdout is
chosen, carry a level and a message, and carry a UTC timestamp unless
timestamps are turned off for deterministic output.

### List
```
list.map(xs, to (x) give back x * 2)  // every member, through a function
list.length([1, 2, 3])                 // 3
length(xs), push(xs, x)                // flat list builtins
```

### Regex
```
regex.match(text, pattern)             // a match record, or nothing
regex.is_match(text, pattern)          // yes/no, searching anywhere
regex.capture(text, pattern, group)    // a captured text, or nothing
regex.replace(text, pattern, "user-$1")// every match, with capture references
regex.split(text, pattern)             // the text between matches
// text.split keeps its literal separator; regex.split is the pattern form.
```

