## Objective
- Complete phase-106: add a dense numeric matrix/tensor value to Redblue, backed by Rust `ndarray`, with elementwise ops, matmul, reductions, shape/indexing, documented promotion rules, tests, docs, and `REPORT.md`.
- Finish with four gates: `cargo fmt --all -- --check`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`, `cargo test --all-targets`, `../rbops/verify.sh "phase-106"`.

## Important Details
- Project root: `/home/runner/work/rbops/rbops/redblue`. Only read/write here; do not inspect the RBOPS pipeline.
- Never touch `.github/workflows/`, `rbops/`, `.opencode/agent/`, or `rbops/phases.json`.
- Do not weaken tests, add ignores/skips, or use `allow(clippy::...)`; phase requires ≥3 new tests, ≥1 `edge_*`, and ≥1 failure-asserting test.
- `must_touch: [src/]`; implementation must land under `src/`.
- Code comments should be avoided unless necessary.
- Use `cargo test <name>` / targeted `--test` during iteration; full suite is long.
- Final command per user prompt is `../rbops/verify.sh "phase-106"` (phase text also mentions `./rbops/verify.sh phase-106`).
- `REPORT.md` must match the AGENTS.md section 4 table shape and include measured binding-vs-nested-list cost.

## Work State
### Completed
- Reproduced original gap with `target/tmp_repro.rb`: `matrix.multiply(...)` failed with `Error: AnalyzerError: Unknown variable 'matrix'`.
- Added `ndarray`: first `cargo add ndarray@0.15 --no-default-features`, then edited `Cargo.toml` to `ndarray = "0.15"`. `Cargo.lock` now includes `ndarray 0.15.6`, `matrixmultiply`, `num-complex`, `num-integer`, `rawpointer`.
- Added `src/matrix.rs` with `Value::Object("matrix", fields)` representation using fields `rows`, `cols`, row-major `data`; avoids changing public `Value` enum.
- Implemented 20 module functions: `zeros`, `ones`, `identity`, `from_lists`, `to_lists`, `shape`, `add`, `subtract`, `multiply`, `divide`, `scale`, `matmul`, `transpose`, `sum`, `mean`, `min`, `max`, `at`, `row`, `column`.
- Shape rules: elementwise ops require exact equal shapes, no broadcasting; errors name both shapes. Matmul requires inner dimensions and names both shapes. Divide-by-zero refused. Empty mean/min/max refused; empty sum is `0`; `0x0`, `Nx0`, `0xN` behavior defined.
- Promotion: all elements are `f64`; integer-looking values promote without truncation; non-finite results are refused with catchable `Runtime` errors.
- Matrix indexes reject negative, fractional, and out-of-range values with catchable errors. Bracket indexing `m[row]` returns a row list via `runtime::index`.
- Max matrix elements: `1_000_000`.
- Integrated:
  - `src/lib.rs`: `mod matrix;`
  - `src/runtime.rs`: early `matrix::builtin` dispatch in `runtime::builtin`; matrix branch in `runtime::index`.
  - `src/value.rs`: matrix display and `type_name() == "matrix"`.
  - `src/stdlib.rs`: `MODULES` includes `"matrix"`; `MODULE_MEMBERS` row; `builtins()` registers all `matrix_*`; `BUILTIN_NAMES`; `BUILTIN_SIGNATURES`.
- Added `tests/matrix_test.rs` with 10 tests, all passing. Includes hand-written matmul, literal elementwise/reduction assertions, `edge_zero_by_zero_matrix_has_defined_behaviour`, shape mismatch, mixed int/float promotion, precision/overflow, out-of-bounds/type mismatch, indexing, dimension limit, and both-engine data equality.
- Added docs:
  - `SPEC.md`: new `### matrix` section before `## Iteration and memoisation`, states binding to `ndarray`, promotion, no broadcasting, empty matrices, indexing, cost.
  - `README.md`: new `### Matrix` section before `## Project Structure`.
- Updated `tests/doc_blocks_runs.txt`: `SPEC.md:1968` → `SPEC.md:2033`, `SPEC.md:1994` → `SPEC.md:2059`.
